# shir_nodes/address_of.node — AddressOf: reference-taking (`&x`).
#
# GENERIC (Go &x, Zig &x, C-like frontends). The IR passes VALUES; what
# "taking an address" means is backend-defined:
#   - backends with real references render a genuine reference
#     (Perl: \(...) / \(...) — aliasing preserved);
#   - value-only backends (JS/ESTree) use SNAPSHOT semantics: the
#     current value passes through. Writes through such a reference are
#     NOT representable there — a frontend must refuse them at its own
#     gate (Refuse > guess), not mis-lower.
# Deref is the matching read side; keep the pair's contract in sync.

node AddressOf
tag "AddressOf"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field operand: expr
